  "body": "Hello,\r\n\r\nI start installing a Synapse server. I managed to install a Synapse server with different users. Different users of the same server (server-name : `nexus_chat1.nexus`) can communicate with each other. Now, I want these users to be able to communicate with other users of another Synapse server (server-name : `nexus_chat2.nexus`).\r\n\r\nI then wanted to follow the [Setting up federation](https://github.com/matrix-org/synapse#setting-up-federation). but I do not understand how to achieve this part:\r\n\r\n> To use a SRV record, first create your SRV record and publish it in DNS. This should have the format _matrix._tcp. <Yourdomain.com> <ttl> IN SRV 10 0 <port> <synapse.server.name>.\r\n\r\nFor my part, when I executed this command: `dig -t srv _matrix._tcp.nexus_chat1.nexus`\r\nI get this: \r\n`;; ANSWER SECTION:`\r\n`_matrix._tcp.nexus_chat1.nexus. 3599 IN SRV 10 10 0 your-dns-needs-immediate-attention.nexus.`\r\n\r\nIf anyone can explain to me how to configure a federation ..",
